    "name": "maximum_area_three_marker_bbox",
    "description": "Draw the largest-area bounding box supported by any three markers, erasing interior marks. Ties retain the first row-major triple.",
    "motivation": "The canonical construction has three rectangle-corner markers; this rule keeps using only three markers when more appear.",
    "program": "(rule!\n  (let* ((cells (filter-cells g (lambda (r c v) (not (= v 0)))))\n         (n (length cells)))\n    (if (empty? cells)\n        g\n        (let* ((groups\n                 (if (< n 3)\n                     (list cells)\n                     (for*/list ([i (in-range n)]\n                                 [j (in-range (+ i 1) n)]\n                                 [k (in-range (+ j 1) n)])\n                       (list (list-ref cells i) (list-ref cells j) (list-ref cells k)))))\n               (boxes (map bbox-of-cells groups))\n               (area (lambda (b)\n                       (* (+ 1 (- (third b) (first b)))\n                          (+ 1 (- (fourth b) (second b))))))\n               (bb (first (sort boxes (lambda (a b) (> (area a) (area b))))))\n               (color (at g (first (first cells)) (second (first cells))))\n               (r0 (first bb)) (c0 (second bb)) (r1 (third bb)) (c1 (fourth bb))\n               (outline\n                 (append\n                   (for/list ([c (in-range c0 (+ c1 1))]) (list r0 c))\n                   (for/list ([c (in-range c0 (+ c1 1))]) (list r1 c))\n                   (for/list ([r (in-range r0 (+ r1 1))]) (list r c0))\n                   (for/list ([r (in-range r0 (+ r1 1))]) (list r c1)))))\n          (paint-cells (empty-grid (rows g) (cols g) 0) outline color)))))"
  },
